; `ne` — the comparison operator that answered `nothing` for every input.
;
; Found 2026-07-28 while measuring fkwu's reference surface to teach the walkers
; axiom-1's third state. `ne` was absent from the rewrite table in
; flatten/gen-source-walker-table.fk, so it matched no op at all and recovered to
; `nothing` (axiom-5). And because `nothing` is truthy in fkwu, every
; `(if (ne x y) A B)` took the then-branch regardless of x and y:
;
;     (ne 1 2)              -> nothing      should be 1
;     (ne 1 1)              -> nothing      should be 0
;     (if (ne 1 1) 42 0)    -> 42           should be 0   <- the whole defect in one line
;
; Three bands exercised `ne` and stayed green on that truthiness. eq-shape-band's own
; header documents "Verdict 524287" and it was returning 524271 — exactly its c4 `ne`
; bit dark, silently red and unnoticed.
;
; Fixed as a DATA row rather than a C edit, which is what that generator's own contract
; says: `ne(a,b) = if(eq a b) 0 1`, the same shape `gt` already uses over `le`. One row
; added to the generated header, zero lines added to runtime/fkwu-uni.c.
;
; Five digits, low to high: ne answers 1 when its arguments differ; 0 when they agree;
; the branch it guards now follows its arguments; it composes through arithmetic the way
; eq-shape-band's c4 always intended; and it agrees with eq's negation on every pair.
;
; Self-contained — kernel verbs only, no preludes.
; witnessed: 2026-07-28 -> 11111, four-way (go/rust/ts all 11111)
(do
    (add (add (add (add
        (if (eq (ne 1 2) 1) 1 0)
        (if (eq (ne 1 1) 0) 10 0))
        (if (eq (if (ne 1 1) 42 0) 0) 100 0))
        (if (eq (sub (ne 1 2) (ne 2 2)) 1) 1000 0))
        (if (eq (ne 5 5) (if (eq 5 5) 0 1)) 10000 0)))
